### Shipping Microservice API - Sample Requests
### Use with VS Code REST Client extension or IntelliJ HTTP Client

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8082

### ========================================
### SHIPPING QUOTE SCENARIOS
### cost = 100 + 50/kg + 25/item + distance-zone surcharge (x2.5 international)
### ========================================

### Local delivery - iPhone from Colombo to Colombo => 625 LKR
POST {{baseUrl}}/quotes
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "branchId": "BRANCH-COL",
    "destinationAddress": {
        "line1": "12 Marine Drive",
        "city": "Colombo",
        "area": "Colombo 04",
        "country": "Sri Lanka"
    },
    "items": [
        { "itemId": "IPHONE-15-001", "quantity": 1 }
    ]
}

###

### Long-haul - iPhone from Jaffna to Colombo (~400 km) => 20125 LKR
### The "landed-cost flip": cheaper sticker at Jaffna, but this shipping reverses it.
POST {{baseUrl}}/quotes
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "branchId": "BRANCH-JAF",
    "destinationAddress": {
        "line1": "12 Marine Drive",
        "city": "Colombo",
        "area": "Colombo 04",
        "country": "Sri Lanka"
    },
    "items": [
        { "itemId": "IPHONE-15-001", "quantity": 1 }
    ]
}

###

### Multi-item - 3 MacBook Neo from Colombo to Colombo => 675 LKR
POST {{baseUrl}}/quotes
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "branchId": "BRANCH-COL",
    "destinationAddress": {
        "line1": "42 Galle Road",
        "city": "Colombo",
        "area": "Colombo 03",
        "country": "Sri Lanka"
    },
    "items": [
        { "itemId": "MACBOOK-NEO-001", "quantity": 3 }
    ]
}

###

### With weight - MacBook Pro from Colombo to Kandy (~115 km, 2.1 kg)
### 100 + (2.1 x 50) + 25 + 5000 = 5230 LKR
POST {{baseUrl}}/quotes
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "branchId": "BRANCH-COL",
    "destinationAddress": {
        "line1": "789 Peradeniya Road",
        "city": "Kandy",
        "area": "Kandy Central",
        "country": "Sri Lanka"
    },
    "items": [
        { "itemId": "MACBOOK-PRO-001", "quantity": 1, "weightKg": 2.1 }
    ]
}

###

### International - MacBook Neo from Colombo to Dubai => 12812.50 LKR (x2.5)
POST {{baseUrl}}/quotes
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "branchId": "BRANCH-COL",
    "destinationAddress": {
        "line1": "1 Sheikh Zayed Rd",
        "city": "Dubai",
        "area": "Downtown",
        "country": "UAE"
    },
    "items": [
        { "itemId": "MACBOOK-NEO-001", "quantity": 1 }
    ]
}

###

### Validation error - missing branchId (should return 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/quotes
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "destinationAddress": {
        "line1": "123 Galle Road",
        "city": "Colombo",
        "area": "Colombo 03",
        "country": "Sri Lanka"
    },
    "items": [
        { "itemId": "IPHONE-15-001", "quantity": 1 }
    ]
}

### ========================================
### SHIPPING CONFIRMATION ENDPOINTS
### ========================================

### Confirm shipping (replace with a real quoteId from a quote above)
POST {{baseUrl}}/confirmations
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "quoteId": "REPLACE-WITH-ACTUAL-QUOTE-ID",
    "orderId": "ORDER-001",
    "customerId": "CUST-001"
}

###

### Confirm shipping - Invalid quote (should return 404)
POST {{baseUrl}}/confirmations
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "quoteId": "INVALID-QUOTE-ID",
    "orderId": "ORDER-002",
    "customerId": "CUST-002"
}

###

### Confirm shipping - Validation error (missing orderId, should return 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/confirmations
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "quoteId": "QUOTE-12345",
    "customerId": "CUST-001"
}

### ========================================
### ACTUATOR ENDPOINTS
### ========================================

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health
Accept: application/json

###

### Application info
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/info
Accept: application/json
